{"id":"CVE-2010-0731","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2010-03-26T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T00:59:39.012Z","description":"The gnutls_x509_crt_get_serial function in the GnuTLS library before 1.2.1, when running on big-endian, 64-bit platforms, calls the asn1_read_value with a pointer to the wrong data type and the wrong length value, which allows remote attackers to bypass the certificate revocation list (CRL) check and cause a stack-based buffer overflow via a crafted X.509 certificate, related to extraction of a serial number.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2010-0167.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2010:0167"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/39127","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"39127"},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2010:089","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2010:089"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/38959","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"38959"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2010/0713","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2010-0713"},{"url":"https://oval.cisecurity.org/repository/search/definition/oval%3Aorg.mitre.oval%3Adef%3A9759","tags":["vdb-entry","signature","x_refsource_OVAL"],"name":"oval:org.mitre.oval:def:9759"},{"url":"http://thread.gmane.org/gmane.comp.encryption.gpg.gnutls.devel/4230","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=573028","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2010-08/msg00001.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SR:2010:014"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2010/1054","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2010-1054"}],"vendors":["cr